  "summary": "Alcaraz leads the career head-to-head with Sinner 10 wins to 7 across 17 matches. On clay the record is 3 wins to 2 for Alcaraz in 5 matches, a small sample, and Sinner won the most recent one, the 2026 Monte Carlo final. Both have strong clay records since 2024-10-26: Sinner 29-3 and Alcaraz 27-2. Sinner has the better serve numbers and Alcaraz has a slightly better return rate.",
  "strengths": [
   "Alcaraz won 93.1% of his clay matches (27 of 29) from 2024-10-26 to 2026-10-26.",
   "His first serve goes in more often than Sinner's: 65.7% against 61.4% (29 and 32 clay matches).",
   "His return points won on clay are 45.1% (29 matches), against Sinner's 44.4% (32 matches).",
   "He converts break points on clay at 46.2% (132 of 286).",
   "He has won 9 of his last 10 matches, all on hard courts in his recent run, including the Vienna title.",
   "He leads the clay head-to-head 3-2 (small sample), including the 2025 Roland Garros final and the 2025 Rome final."
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
   "His second serve is weaker than Sinner's on clay: 56.5% of points won, against 60.4%.",
   "His service points won on clay are 64.5%, against Sinner's 69.8%.",
   "He averages 2.5 aces per match on clay, against Sinner's 4.5.",
   "He saves 65.7% of break points on clay (111 of 169), and faces more of them than Sinner (169 against 107).",
   "He lost the most recent clay meeting, the 2026 Monte Carlo final, 7-6(5) 6-3."
  ],
  "game_plan": [
   "Attack Alcaraz's second serve. He wins 56.5% of second-serve points on clay, against 60.4% for Sinner. Step in and return aggressively.",
   "Hold serve through the first serve. Sinner wins 75.7% of first-serve points on clay and averages 4.5 aces per match, against Alcaraz's 2.5, so shorter service games put pressure on Alcaraz.",
   "Create break-point chances. Alcaraz has faced 169 break points on clay and saved 65.7% of them. Sinner's own save rate is 64.5% (107 faced), so he should expect tight service games too.",
   "Repeat the Monte Carlo approach from April 2026, the latest clay meeting: Sinner won 7-6(5) 6-3. The clay record overall favors Alcaraz, so don't rely on past results alone.",
   "Raise the first-serve percentage. Sinner gets 61.4% of first serves in on clay, against Alcaraz's 65.7%, and each extra first serve avoids a weaker second-serve point."
